## A pile of cards, e.g. a game's stock or its discards
// The game that uses these cards names its piles, and says what each kind of pile takes.
// A drawable list:  its element holds its cards' elements, e.g. `<cards-pile>` around `<cards-card>`s.
a "pile" is a drawable list of cards where:
	// what the game calls it, e.g. "stock"
	- its "name" is text
	// the color and value of its last card:  what the next card goes on
	- its "color" is:
		"none" if it is empty
		the color of its last card otherwise
	- its "value" is:
		0 if it is empty
		the value of its last card otherwise
	// its name, then each card's state, e.g. "stock: Q♠️+ 7♥️—"
	- its "state" is:
		set state to (its name or "pile") + ":"
		for each card in the pile
			set state to state + " " + the state of the card
		return state

// a card is in one pile at a time:  putting it on another pile takes it off this one
a card belongs to one pile


## Tests
to test piles
	set the stock to a new pile with name = "stock"
	set the discards to a new pile with name = "discards"
	the color of the stock should be "none"
	the value of the stock should be 0

	add (a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is up) to the stock
	add (a new card whose rank is 7, suit is hearts and direction is down) to the stock
	the color of the stock should be red
	the value of the stock should be 7
	the state of the stock should be "stock: Q♠️+ 7♥️—"

	// a card is in one pile at a time
	set the card to the last card of the stock
	add the card to the discards
	the number of cards in the stock should be 1
	the pile of the card is the discards should be yes
	the state of the discards should be "discards: 7♥️—"
